      "title": "Why these panels may be empty",
      "description": "Instrumented-but-inactive IPC and support metrics; privacy guarantees.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 37
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Expected to be empty on a freshly started stack.**\n\nAll IPC and support-export metrics are instrumented in production code but were **not observed** during Phase 33.3 verification: no named-pipe client connected and no support bundle was exported in the sampled window.\n\n- `irandirect_ipc_requests_total`, `irandirect_ipc_request_duration_milliseconds_*`\n- `irandirect_support_bundles_exported_total`, `irandirect_support_bundles_failed_total`, `irandirect_support_bundle_duration_milliseconds_*`\n\nPanels populate as soon as the CLI or tray issues an IPC command or exports a bundle. Empty means *no activity*, not a broken query.\n\n**Privacy:** the `ipc_command` label is bounded to a fixed command vocabulary. No request or response payload, output path, or pipe content is ever labelled or displayed - the telemetry contract forbids it and no such label exists on any live series."
      }
    }
